# Composite (ADR-009): a container image that is BOTH run as root AND has no
# healthcheck is an unhardened image worth escalating past either leaf alone.
# Gated on the `docker` fact so it never runs in a repo without a Dockerfile
# (most-discriminating-first). The leaves (KEUR-IAC-002/003) still fire on their
# own; this composite only combines their evidence and raises the signal.
#
# This is the reference composite: engine stays dumb, the "root AND no-healthcheck
# matters" logic is DATA here, not C++.
# @see docs/adr/ADR-009-composite-rules-and-facts.md
# @implements ADR-009.composite
id: KEUR-IAC-010
maturity: 2
title: Unhardened container image (runs as root and has no healthcheck)
category: iac
severity: warning
engine: composite
action: warn
confidence: 0.6
requires:
  framework: docker
composite:
  all: KEUR-IAC-002 KEUR-IAC-003
message: "Unhardened container image: it runs as root AND declares no HEALTHCHECK. Add a non-root USER and a HEALTHCHECK — either alone is a warning, both together is a hardening gap."
fix: "Add both a non-root USER and a HEALTHCHECK instruction to the Dockerfile."
